.TH PSPP 1 "2026-11-11" "pspp 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pspp \- interactive and scriptable process memory viewer grouped by parent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pspp
.RB [ \-\-update\-ms
.IR MS ]
.br
.B pspp
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ PATTERN ]
.br
.B pspp \-\-query
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pspp
("ps plus plus") sums memory used by running processes grouped by their parent
process
.RI ( "pid <- ppid" ),
exposing the true memory footprint of multi-process applications such as
browsers, WebView/Electron apps, build tools, and worker supervisors.
.PP
When invoked on an interactive terminal with no query-mode arguments,
.B pspp
opens a live, mouse-enabled terminal interface inspired by
.BR btop (1)
with braille memory history graphs, a grass-green to bloody-red usage gradient,
and an expandable process tree.
When
.IR PATTERN ,
.BR \-\-pid ,
.BR \-\-min ,
.BR \-\-top ,
.B \-\-json
or
.B \-\-query
is provided\(emor when standard output is piped or redirected\(em\fBpspp\fR
runs a single snapshot in non-interactive query mode, prints a plain table or
JSON document to standard output, and exits.
Query mode is deterministic: it never reads
.IR pspp.conf ;
its defaults are
.BR "\-\-mem rss" ,
.BR "\-\-agg rollup" ,
.BR "\-\-sort agg"
and binary units.
The plain header
.RB ( "RSS \(*S (rollup)" )
and the JSON output name the mode in effect.
.PP
.BR \-\-mem ,
.BR \-\-agg ,
.BR \-\-sort ,
.B \-\-base10
and
.B \-\-update\-ms
apply to whichever mode runs.
In the TUI they override
.I pspp.conf
for that run only and are never saved; with
.B save_on_exit
only settings changed inside the TUI are written.
.SS Aggregation Modes
.TP
.B rollup
Sums each process together with all of its descendants (children,
grandchildren, and deeper).
Default in both TUI and query mode.
.TP
.B flat
Sums only direct children under each parent process, keeping parent and child
layers separate.
.PP
In query mode, the final
.B TOTAL
row (and JSON
.BR total )
counts every process covered by the returned rows at most once: in
.B rollup
mode, rows that already have an ancestor in the returned set are not added a
second time.
.SS Memory Metrics and Approximate Values
Depending on the platform,
.B pspp
supports:
.TP
.B rss
Resident Set Size: RAM the process is using right now, including shared pages
also mapped by other processes (macOS and Linux; default).
.TP
.B vsz
Virtual Size: total virtual address space reserved by the process, most of
which is not backed by physical RAM (macOS and Linux).
.TP
.B footprint
Apple's physical footprint
.RI ( ri_phys_footprint
via
.BR proc_pid_rusage ),
matching Activity Monitor's Memory column (macOS only).
.TP
.B pss
Proportional Set Size from
.IR /proc/<pid>/smaps_rollup :
RAM used with shared pages divided evenly across sharing processes (Linux
only).
.TP
.B uss
Unique Set Size
.RI ( "Private_Clean + Private_Dirty" ):
RAM private to a single process\(emroughly what killing it frees immediately
(Linux only).
.TP
.B swap
Swapped-out bytes reported by
.I /proc/<pid>/smaps_rollup
(Linux only).
.PP
When per-process privileged metrics are unreadable without elevated permissions,
.B pspp
keeps the process in the snapshot and appends a trailing tilde
.RB ( ~ )
to indicate that a value or aggregated sum is approximate.
On macOS without root privileges, processes owned by other users have
unreadable parent info via
.B proc_pidinfo
and appear as top-level roots.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I PATTERN
Case-insensitive substring filter matched against process command names
.RB ( COMM ).
Triggers non-interactive query mode.
Regex-style
.B !
prefixes are not currently supported.
.TP
.BI \-\-pid " PID"
Restrict query output to
.I PID
and its descendant subtree.
Triggers query mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-mem " KIND"
Select memory metric:
.BR rss ,
.BR vsz ,
.B footprint
(macOS), or
.BR pss ,
.BR uss ,
.B swap
(Linux).
Applies to both TUI and query mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-agg " MODE"
Select aggregation mode:
.B rollup
or
.BR flat .
Applies to both TUI and query mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-min " SIZE"
Filter out rows whose aggregated memory is below
.IR SIZE .
Accepts byte integers or binary unit suffixes (case-insensitive):
.BR B ,
.BR K / KB / KiB ,
.BR M / MB / MiB ,
.BR G / GB / GiB ,
.BR T / TB / TiB ,
.BR P / PB / PiB
(for example,
.BR 512K ,
.BR 100M ,
.BR 1.5G ).
Triggers query mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-sort " FIELD"
Sort query rows by
.B agg
(aggregated memory, descending),
.B own
(own memory, descending),
.B pid
(ascending), or
.B comm
(case-insensitive ascending).
Ties break by ascending PID.
Applies to both TUI and query mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-top " N"
Show at most
.I N
rows after sorting
.RI ( N
must be at least 1).
Triggers query mode.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Format query output as pretty-printed JSON
.RB ( "{ ""mem"": ""rss"", ""agg"": ""rollup"", ""rows"": [...], ""total"": <bytes> }" )
with raw integer byte values; each row also carries
.B pct
(aggregated memory as a percentage of total RAM, one decimal).
Triggers query mode.
.TP
.B \-\-query
Force one-shot query mode even when standard output is a terminal.
.TP
.BI "\-f, \-\-filter " TEXT
Pre-set the TUI process filter (like
.BR "btop \-f" ).
In query mode it is used as
.I PATTERN
when none is given.
.TP
.B \-\-base10
Format human-readable sizes using decimal powers of 1000
.RB ( KB / MB / GB )
instead of binary powers of 1024
.RB ( KiB / MiB / GiB ).
Applies to both TUI and query mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-update\-ms " MS"
Refresh interval in milliseconds for interactive TUI mode, clamped to
.BR 100 .. 86400000
(default:
.BR 2000 ,
or
.B update_ms
from
.IR pspp.conf ).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print short
.RB ( \-h )
or detailed
.RB ( \-\-help )
usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
The interactive TUI supports keyboard control across all views and overlays:
.SS Navigation
.TP
.B Up/Down, j/k
Move selection one row.
.TP
.B PgUp/PgDn
Move selection by one page.
.TP
.B Home/End, g/G
Jump to first or last visible row.
.TP
.B q/Q, Ctrl\-C, Ctrl\-Q
Quit
.B pspp
.RB ( Ctrl\-C
and
.B Ctrl\-Q
quit immediately from any mode or overlay).
.TP
.B f/F, /
Start interactive
.B COMM
substring filter input.
.TP
.B c/C
Clear the committed filter.
.TP
.B Esc
Open the main menu overlay
.RB ( Options " / " Help " / " Quit ).
.SS Tree Controls
.TP
.B Space, Enter
Toggle expand/collapse on the selected process node.
.TP
.B Left
Collapse the selected node if expanded, otherwise jump to its parent node.
.TP
.B Right
Expand the selected node.
.SS Display & Filter Input
.TP
.B e/E
Toggle aggregation mode between
.B rollup
and
.BR flat .
.TP
.B m/M
Cycle through memory metrics available on the current OS.
.TP
.B s
Cycle sort key
.RB ( agg " -> " own " -> " pid " -> " comm ).
.TP
.B S, r/R
Reverse sort direction.
.TP
.B Filter input
Type printable characters (including spaces);
.B Backspace
deletes one character;
.B Enter
commits the filter;
.B Esc
clears the filter and exits filter input.
.SS Menu, Options, and Help Overlays
.TP
.B Menu: Up/Down, j/k, Tab, Shift\-Tab
Move between
.BR Options ,
.BR Help ,
and
.BR Quit .
.TP
.B Menu: Enter, Space
Activate the selected menu button.
.TP
.B Menu: Esc, q/Q
Close the menu and return to the process table.
.TP
.B Options: Up/Down, j/k
Select a setting row.
.TP
.B Options: Left/Right
Cycle or toggle the selected setting
.RB ( update_ms
steps by +/-100 ms).
.TP
.B Options: Enter
Open the numeric editor on
.B update_ms
(digits append,
.B Backspace
deletes,
.B Enter
commits,
.B Esc
cancels) or advance other settings.
.TP
.B Options: Esc, q/Q
Close Options and return to the menu.
.TP
.B Help: Up/Down, j/k, PgUp/PgDn
Scroll help text;
.B Esc
or
.B q/Q
closes Help and returns to the menu.
.SS Mouse Actions
.TP
.B Wheel up/down
Scroll process selection by 3 rows.
.TP
.B Left click row
Select row.
.TP
.B Left click [+]/[\-] or double\-click row
Toggle expand/collapse on that node.
.TP
.B Menu click
Click a menu button to activate it; click outside the menu box to close it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
In query mode,
.B pspp
uses
.BR grep (1)-style
exit codes:
.TP
.B 0
At least one matching row was printed (an early closed pipe on stdout, such as
.BR "pspp | head" ,
also exits 0).
In TUI mode, clean exit returns 0.
.TP
.B 1
Query matched zero rows (plain mode also prints
.B "no matches"
to standard error;
.B \-\-json
prints
.BR "{""mem"":""rss"",""agg"":""rollup"",""rows"":[],""total"":0}" ).
In TUI mode, terminal initialization/runtime failure returns 1.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error (invalid option, unknown/unavailable
.BR \-\-mem ,
bad
.B \-\-min
size, or
.BR "\-\-top 0" )
or standard output write error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $PSPP_CONFIG_DIR/pspp.conf
Overrides the default configuration file location when
.B PSPP_CONFIG_DIR
is set and non-empty.
.TP
.I ~/.config/pspp/pspp.conf
Default TOML configuration file on Linux (or
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/pspp/pspp.conf ).
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/pspp/pspp.conf
Default TOML configuration file on macOS (via platform config directory lookup).
.PP
Supported TOML keys:
.BR update_ms ,
.BR mem_kind ,
.BR agg_mode ,
.BR graph_symbol ,
.BR base10 ,
.BR save_on_exit ,
.BR sort_key ,
and
.BR sort_reverse .
When
.B save_on_exit
is
.B true
(default), TUI option changes are saved atomically via a temporary sibling file
on exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Launch the interactive TUI with default settings:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
pspp
.fi
.RE
.PP
Print the top 5 process subtrees by Resident Set Size:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
pspp \-\-top 5
.fi
.RE
.PP
Find processes matching "chrome" whose subtree uses at least 200 MiB:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
pspp chrome \-\-min 200M
.fi
.RE
.PP
Inspect direct-child memory on macOS using physical footprint:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
pspp \-\-mem footprint \-\-agg flat \-\-top 10
.fi
.RE
.PP
Emit JSON for a specific PID subtree and extract total bytes with
.BR jq (1):
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
pspp \-\-pid 1 \-\-json | jq '.total'
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ps (1),
.BR pgrep (1),
.BR top (1),
.BR btop (1)
